### Fonts in the panel - SIL Open Font License 1.1

The `.ttf` files under `PrismaUI/views/SpellLearning/SpellLearningPanel/themes/fonts/book/` and
`PrismaUI/views/SpellLearning/SpellLearningPanel/themes/chalkboard/fonts/` are subsets of open fonts under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Google Fonts families, LXGW Xiaolai, and Hakgyoansim Bunpil by KERIS, designed by
Yoon Design). Each font's license sits next to it (`<Family>-OFL.txt`, and `HakgyoansimBunpil-LICENSE.txt` for
the KERIS font), and the `README.txt` in each folder names every file's source font and license.

### PrismaUI API header

`plugins/PrismaUI_API.h` is the API header the PrismaUI framework
(<https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/148718>) provides for other mods to copy into their projects.

### Immersive Spell Learning - DESTified patch script (`optional/ISLPatch`)

`optional/ISLPatch/Scripts/Source/DEST_ISL_PlayerSpellLearningScript.psc` and its compiled `.pex` are a
modified version of the study script from:

- **"Immersive Spell Learning - DESTified" v1.4.5 by Hackfield**
  (<https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/45514>) - the base script. Its Nexus permissions allow
  modification and improved releases with credit. It credits, in turn, **Ameisenfutter** (the original
  Immersive Spell Learning) and **Parapets** (Don't Eat Spell Tomes).
- **"I Just Want to Sit Down and Read" by GiraPomba**
  (<https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/121282>) - the sit-down study animation code (GPMA/OAR,
  ImprovedCameraSE and TrueDirectionalMovement support). Its Nexus permissions allow modification, with credit
  on upload.
- **Gate to Sovngarde CE Bookworm trait support** - compatibility code only: the script checks whether GTS CE's
  Bookworm trait effect is on the player and shortens study time. No GTS CE files or scripts are included.

Heart of Magic's study hooks and a save-load re-registration fix are added. This script is third-party work: it
is not under this project's MIT license and belongs to its original authors; it is released here as a modified
patch as their Nexus permissions allow, with the credit above.

## Corresponding Source

The complete Corresponding Source for the DLLs is public at
<https://github.com/Iwillbewarlock/HeartOfMagic>, tag `v@PROJECT_VERSION@` (the tag of this release).
CommonLibSSE-NG is its git submodule `plugins/external/commonlibsse-ng` at tag `v10.0.0`
(<https://github.com/alandtse/CommonLibVR>, branch `ng`); `git submodule update --init --recursive`
fetches it. The third-party libraries below come from the vcpkg manifest `vcpkg.json`. Building:
`BuildRelease.ps1` (see the repository's README and CLAUDE.md).

## Libraries in the DLLs

Linked statically or compiled in from headers (vcpkg triplet `x64-windows-static`). Their license
texts are in `licenses/`.

| Library | Version | License | License text |
|---|---|---|---|
| CommonLibSSE-NG | 10.0.0 | GPL-3.0-or-later + Modding Exception + GPL-3.0 Linking Exception | `licenses/CommonLibSSE-NG/COPYING.txt`, `licenses/CommonLibSSE-NG/EXCEPTIONS.md` |
| CommonLibSSE (the original code by Ryan-rsm-McKenzie that CommonLibSSE-NG grew from) | - | MIT (kept for attribution) | `licenses/CommonLibSSE-NG/LICENSE-MIT.txt` |
| {fmt} | 12.1.0 | MIT | `licenses/fmt.txt` |
| spdlog | 1.17.0 | MIT | `licenses/spdlog.txt` |
| JSON for Modern C++ (nlohmann-json) | 3.12.0 | MIT | `licenses/nlohmann-json.txt` |
| rapidcsv | 8.90 | BSD-3-Clause | `licenses/rapidcsv.txt` |
| Xbyak | 7.28 | BSD-3-Clause | `licenses/xbyak.txt` |
| DirectXMath | 2025-04-03 | MIT | `licenses/directxmath.txt` |
| DirectX Tool Kit (DirectXTK) | 2025-10-27 | MIT | `licenses/directxtk.txt` |
| RapidFuzz (rapidfuzz-cpp) | 3.3.3 | MIT | `licenses/rapidfuzz-cpp.txt` |
| Highway | 1.3.0 | Apache-2.0 | `licenses/highway.txt` |

The Microsoft C/C++ runtime (CRT) is linked statically under the Visual Studio redistribution terms.
`SpellLearning.dll` also uses Microsoft's OpenMP runtime, `vcomp140.dll`, which is not in the zip: it comes
with the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable, which Skyrim and SKSE setups already have.
